trusttunnel_client-authkey-mipsel — TrustTunnel client for MIPS (mipsel) Keenetic routers
with client_random_auth_key support. Built by the TrustTunnel-Keenetic-Native project.

This binary contains software from:

  TrustTunnel Client — https://github.com/TrustTunnel/TrustTunnelClient
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSE-Apache-2.0).

  OpenSSL 4.0.2 — https://www.openssl.org/
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSE-Apache-2.0).
  Includes the MIPS build patch from AdGuard's NativeLibsCommon recipes.

Modifications (Apache-2.0, section 4b) — the full diffs are in patches/:

  patches/openssl-0002-custom-client-random-and-hkdf.patch
    OpenSSL: SSL_set_custom_client_random() — a caller-supplied 32-byte ClientRandom in the
    TLS 1.3 ClientHello (refused for DTLS and for TLS below 1.3), copied by SSL_dup();
    and <openssl/hkdf.h> with a BoringSSL-compatible HKDF() on top of EVP_PKEY HKDF.

  patches/client-0001-auth-key-with-openssl.patch
    TrustTunnel client: build the auth key code with OpenSSL (deprecated low-level AES
    allowed, the HKDF argument-order warning skipped when the compatible HKDF is present).

Sources of the released build: TrustTunnelClient commit 7bde23f (1.3.0 + 2 commits).
